This file contains more detailed doctests for the stdnum.in_.tan module. It
tries to cover more corner cases and detailed functionality that is not
really useful as module documentation.

>>> from stdnum.in_ import tan
>>> from stdnum.exceptions import *

Test valid TAN numbers.

>>> numbers = '''
... AABB123456
... ABCD123456
... WXYY999999
... MFHG000123
...
... '''
>>> [x for x in numbers.splitlines() if x and not tan.is_valid(x)]
[]

Test lower case is converted to upper case.

>>> tan.validate('abcd123456')
'ABCD123456'
>>> tan.validate('AbCd123456')
'ABCD123456'

Test invalid lengths.

>>> tan.validate('ABCD12345')
Traceback (most recent call last):
    ...
InvalidLength: ...
>>> tan.validate('ABCD1234567')
Traceback (most recent call last):
    ...
InvalidLength: ...

Test invalid format (non-alphabetic in first 4 positions).

>>> tan.validate('1234ABCD56')
Traceback (most recent call last):
    ...
InvalidFormat: ...
>>> tan.validate('ABCD1234AB')
Traceback (most recent call last):
    ...
InvalidFormat: ...

Test invalid characters O, I, Q in first 4 positions.

>>> tan.validate('OBCX123456')
Traceback (most recent call last):
    ...
InvalidComponent: ...
>>> tan.is_valid('OBCX123456')
False
>>> tan.is_valid('ABCD123456')
True

Test format function.

>>> tan.format(' ABCD123456 ')
'ABCD123456'
>>> tan.format('abcd 123456')
'ABCD123456'